From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Chagas <drochachagas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:57:59 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Layers dock: list each layer's effects under it, with eye
 toggles

Like Photoshop's Layers panel, a layer with filters gets an expander
(collapsed by default) and child rows: "Effects", whose eye turns all of
them on or off, then one row per effect with its own eye. Layer Style
effects are listed once each in Photoshop's order (one row even when an
effect is drawn by two filters, as a centered stroke is), other filters
after them in GIMP's order. Double-click an effect: the Layer Style
dialog on that effect (any other filter: GIMP's Layer Effects editor).

Design: effect rows store their layer's own view renderer, so all code
reading a row as "an item" keeps seeing the layer (clicking an effect
row selects its layer, as in Photoshop). New model columns mark item and
effect rows; the item's eye, lock, thumbnail and editable name cells are
hidden on effect rows, which show their own eye, icon and label. Effect
rows refuse drops. Rows are refreshed on "filters-changed" (also emitted
when a filter is toggled or edited); the expanded state is kept on the
drawable, so live previews that replace filters keep the rows open.
Group layers keep only GIMP's fx popover (their child rows are layers).

GimpContainerTreeView's model_columns array was a fixed 16 and the
Layers list already used 13: raised to 32
(GIMP_CONTAINER_TREE_VIEW_MAX_COLUMNS) and
gimp_container_tree_store_columns_add() now refuses to write past it.

Files: gimpdrawabletreeview.c (the feature), gimpcontainertreeview.h and
gimpcontainertreestore.c (column limit).

Test: a text layer with a Layer Style: expander shows, collapsed; expand,
toggle an effect's eye and the Effects eye, double-click an effect, move
and delete the layer and undo.

Closes: https://github.com/diegochagas/gimphoto/issues/6

